---
module: resource_loading
func_id: look-up-files
---

***conformance tests***

# first-dir-wins
With `notes.md` in both directories `first` and `second`, resolving `notes.md` over [first, second] gives `first/notes.md`.

# later-dir-is-searched
With `notes.md` only in `second`, resolving `notes.md` over [first, second] gives `second/notes.md`, and finding gives the directory `second`.

# missing-file
Resolving and finding `missing.md` over a directory without it give none, and reading gives none.

# parent-relative-path
With `shared.md` in `root` and the directory `root/plain`, resolving `../shared.md` over [root/plain] gives `root/plain/../shared.md`.

# directory-hides-later-file
With a directory `notes.md` in `first` and a file `notes.md` in `second`, resolving `notes.md` over [first, second] gives `first/notes.md`.

# read-text
With `notes.md` holding `# hello` in `second`, reading `notes.md` over [first, second] gives `# hello`.

***acceptance tests***
